  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9BC1F2">Remark <span data-tag="9BC1F2">3.2.5.5</span>.</a>FF@${\mathfrak F}_{X}(\calC )$ Let $\calC $ be a small $\infty $-category. The construction $f \mapsto \Nerve _{f}(\calC )$ determines a functor from $(\sSet )^{\calC }$ to $(\sSet )_{/ \Nerve (\calC )}$. This functor admits a left adjoint, which we will denote by $X \mapsto {\mathfrak F}_ X(\calC )$ (the existence of this functor follows from the adjoint functor theorem). If $X \rightarrow \Nerve (\calC )$ is a left fibration, then $\calF _{X}(\calC )$ is a functor $\calC \rightarrow \sSet $ which assigns to each $C \in \calC $ a simplicial set which is weakly equivalent to the fiber $X_{C} = X \times _{ \Nerve (\calC )} \{ C\} $; this follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/518091" data-tag="518091">3.2.5.18</a> below. </p>
